    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38527" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōcursĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		procurro, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a running forward</i>, <i>stepping
				forth.</i> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, of an orator: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">procursio opportuna, brevis, moderata, rara,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 3, 126</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a digression</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">necessaria post narrationem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint.
					4, 3, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
